{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness","id":1492849,"title":"Ideas how Qanon or Westboro translate to world of darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-11T19:27:31-07:00","id":1492849,"title":"Ideas how Qanon or Westboro translate to world of darkness","content":"Qanon is a radical cult Westboro is a hateful church that pickets soldiers funerals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T08:35:43-07:00","id":1492883,"title":"","content":"QAnon, to my knowledge are conspiracy theorists and WoD's rife with genuine conspiracies. It would be convenient for the secret masters of the world if the typical factions who claimed that such cabals existed were blatantly incorrect, bigotted and either mouthpieces or useful idiots to a human/sleeper establishment that doesn't want democratically accountable institutions interfering with their affairs. The idea is explored in <i>Shadows of New York</i> and <i>Night Road</i>, even if the latter doesn't name them specifically, although I would expect WoD's books to do so as well. For that matter, it would probably suit the Camarilla or Technocracy if anybody who publically declared their existence could be dismissed a delusional commie, hypothetically speaking.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what relevance the Westboro Baptist Church could have to the unique entities of WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 09-12-2022, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T08:55:31-07:00","id":1492885,"title":"","content":"QAnon is probably close to Incognito. Westboro is human-grown hate; there'll be banes swirling around them in much larger quantities than the background, but they aren't going to be following the lead of a supernatural entity. They only think that they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T13:17:58-07:00","id":1492920,"title":"","content":"Both of these feel like they're best handled with a light touch: reminders that humans are problems without supernaturals being behind what they do, or even being involved at all. It's good to remind ourselves that the World of Darkness can look just like our world because people like this already exist in our supposedly not so dark world.<br /> <br /> To most of the supernatural the existence of these sorts of hate groups are just something humans do. They're dangerous, they're more dangerous if supernaturals decide to help them (or use them anyway), but only the most hubris filled fools would think these types wouldn't turn on some secret monstrous benefactor.<br /> <br /> The fact that these groups exist, despite lots of entities in the WoD being perfectly capable of wiping them out without all the problems humans have to deal with in that regard, is dark enough on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-13-2022, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T02:56:52-07:00","id":1492965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1492920#post1492920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of these feel like they're best handled with a light touch: reminders that humans are problems with supernaturals being behind what they do, or even being involved at all. It's good to remind ourselves that the World of Darkness can look just like our world because people like this already exist in our supposedly not so dark world.<br /> <br /> To most of the supernatural the existence of these sorts of hate groups are just something humans do. They're dangerous, they're more dangerous if supernaturals decide to help them (or use them anyway), but only the most hubris filled fools would think these types wouldn't turn on some secret monstrous benefactor.<br /> <br /> The fact that these groups exist, despite lots of entities in the WoD being perfectly capable of wiping them out without all the problems humans have to deal with in that regard, is dark enough on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. If they have to be in at all, have them ironically devoured by some eldritch evil that can't be bothered dealing with bigots. Even the Malfeans haven't got time for the WBC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T08:35:59-07:00","id":1492977,"title":"","content":"ROFL One thing is how Qanon could stay together in spite off so many failed prophecies.<br /> <br /> in a world with real prophecies","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-13-2022, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T09:20:41-07:00","id":1492982,"title":"","content":"If I'm recalling things correctly, QAnon is a conspiracy theory that most of the world's elites are child molesters and that this molestation might be related to some kind of mystical/satanic cult. In the WoD, this probably has a lot of basis in truth. If I were going to bring up this in a WoD game, I'd make it true (at least for a lot of powerful people) and maybe tie it to some kind of evil WoD faction like the Baali, Nephandi, or Wyrm.<br /> <br /> As for Westboro, I would just have them be a wacky fringe group, kinda like in real life.<br /> <br /> How you portray either group in game, or decide to at all, is going to depend on the tastes of your players too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T09:28:50-07:00","id":1492985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1492982#post1492982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm recalling things correctly, QAnon is a conspiracy theory that most of the world's elites are child molesters and that this molestation might be related to some kind of mystical/satanic cult. In the WoD, this probably has a lot of basis in truth. If I were going to bring up this in a WoD game, I'd make it true (at least for a lot of powerful people) and maybe tie it to some kind of evil WoD faction like the Baali, Nephandi, or Wyrm.<br /> <br /> As for Westboro, I would just have them be a wacky fringe group, kinda like in real life.<br /> <br /> How you portray either group in game, or decide to at all, is going to depend on the tastes of your players too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a bad move when BotW 2e tried doing it with the leftovers of the Satanic Panic, and it would be even worse to do it again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T09:40:28-07:00","id":1492987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1492985#post1492985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a bad move when BotW 2e tried doing it with the leftovers of the Satanic Panic, and it would be even worse to do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t necessarily think that they should include QAnon in any official WoD book, but if I were going to include it at all, I\u2019d make it largely* true since it\u2019s exactly the kind of conspiracies that have been a major part of the WoD since it\u2019s inception. <br /> <br /> What I would include in my game isn\u2019t necessarily what others should include or what should be published. We were asked how to include it and I gave my answer.<br /> <br /> * Largely depending on what specific QAnon claims we\u2019re discussing. If it\u2019s cults of demon worshipping child molesters in positions of power, then it fits in perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T10:03:50-07:00","id":1492991,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it would be a good idea to include any QAnon stuff in a game one way or another. A lot of people have committed very atrocious things because of their insane belief. Saying 'they were right because there actually is a demon cult' is feel is just as bad 'they are doing it because they are being corrupted' or whatever.<br /> <br /> I think just saying &quot;this is a real thing that is happening because humans sometimes just be like this&quot; would be the only way to properly handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T10:16:40-07:00","id":1492994,"title":"","content":"If these groups have no supernatural tie in at all, is there a point in including them? Personally, I think I wouldn\u2019t include them. Sometimes people just want some fiction and putting real politically significant groups into a game has the potential to create unhappiness and strife. <br /> <br /> But, if they were going to be included, seems like there should be at least some link to the group and what the player characters might be doing. <br /> <br /> Back in 1990\u2019s conspiracy theories seemed more apolitical, almost innocent in a sense. Now they carry more political baggage and even some of the core conspiracies that define the WoD are objectionable to some. How does one deal with that? It entirely depends on the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T10:46:39-07:00","id":1492995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1492994#post1492994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If these groups have no supernatural tie in at all, is there a point in including them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the story being told. I can't think on something that would feature them as an aspect of the story but, I don't think that I wouldn't have them as part of a setting especially if the game was taking place in DC. In that same vein I don't think I'd make the Covid-19 supernatural but the effects would still be felt. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1492994#post1492994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think I wouldn\u2019t include them. Sometimes people just want some fiction and putting real politically significant groups into a game has the potential to create unhappiness and strife.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is anything necessarily <i>wrong</i> with that but, if you choose to do so (especially taking real groups that have done terrible things) then treating it well is important. I think giving justification for these groups that is out of their control would be a cheap hook that wouldn't be justifiable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1492994#post1492994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, if they were going to be included, seems like there should be at least some link to the group and what the player characters might be doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again I don't think that would be necessary to do just to include a real event that is on going. Humans being terrible is pretty ok to include without saying that it's because of 'demons' or 'wyrm' or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1492994#post1492994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in 1990\u2019s conspiracy theories seemed more apolitical, almost innocent in a sense. Now they carry more political baggage and even some of the core conspiracies that define the WoD are objectionable to some. How does one deal with that? It entirely depends on the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wouldn't describe the conspiracies as apolitical but, that's not what I'm talking about here.<br /> <br /> CW: Filicide<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> People that believe in QAnon have kidnapped and killed their own children because they believed them to be fake replacements by the deep state. Make a story about how they have a justification for this action because things they believe in are 'real' would be a disservice to the families effected. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T10:57:32-07:00","id":1492997,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not familiar with that particular murder story, though it\u2019s not representative of the claims of QAnon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T11:04:00-07:00","id":1492999,"title":"","content":"It is a result and I'm of the opinion that results matter more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T11:08:08-07:00","id":1493000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1492999#post1492999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a result and I'm of the opinion that results matter more.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one guy. If that is our standard, then Vampire: the Masquerade makes teenagers kill their parents because there was that one incident back in the 1990's. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T11:18:45-07:00","id":1493004,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1493000#post1493000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one guy. If that is our standard, then Vampire: the Masquerade makes teenagers kill their parents because there was that one incident back in the 1990's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's not the fact that it <b>happened</b> it has to do with <b>how the event is framed</b>. If you are going to make QAnon's belief into an actual demon cult, then you are giving justification to these people. You are saying that these people have &quot;stumbled into the truth&quot; and &quot;are trying to wake-up the sheeple.&quot; And no it's not 'just one guy', it's multiple cases.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, if you are saying these people are being manipulated by supernatural beings then you are also giving justification for these events. &quot;It's not their fault, they where being controlled by forced unknown to them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T13:40:34-07:00","id":1493022,"title":"","content":"There's also a massive and important difference in how to treat a work of explicit fiction that one person took too far, and a movement with the goal of spreading violence based on things most people consider fiction.<br /> <br /> If I write a story about a superhero that gained the power to fly via a drug, which I never actually explain how to make, and someone convinces themselves that they've figured out the drug, and then jump off a building and dies? That's tragic but not my fault morally or legally.<br /> <br /> If I find out about that story, and then start selling a drug I claim is the real thing and will let you fly, and even one person gets hurt because of it, I'd be a criminal.<br /> <br /> The goal there matters a lot. QAnon is (however some people theorize its origins) not a game. It's a group that advocates criminal activity and violence as justified by a complex belief system. Label that however you want, it's not a piece of entertainment that one guy took too far.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not just &quot;one guy&quot; with QAnon. The QAnon movement is linked to multiple criminal incidents including kidnappings (yes, plural), false reports of bomb threats, in-person harassment campaigns, countless online harassment campaigns, assaults, and murders. Whatever &quot;standard&quot; you want to set here about how they've crossed whatever line into QAnon being an active danger to the public via radicalizing its members, if that standard is functional, QAnon has met it.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> And going back a bit, the point of including human evil in the WoD that doesn't have supernatural ties is simple: to have the story remember that humans are perfectly capable of evil on their own. Losing sight of what humanity is up to isn't just dangerous because of things like upkeeping the Masquerade, but because humans can be as vicious, violent, and cunning as any supernatural without the help. QAnon might not pose any distinct threats to supernaturals in the WoD at large, but they can easily be a problem to anything that cares about (1) people not being subjected to evil acts of violence, and (2) anything that simply wants to stay hidden in the modern world.<br /> <br /> You can completely avoid everything MrNatas just said, and still have QAnon hackers trying to blackmail celebrities by stealing their personal medical histories (something that's happened) cause a bit problem for a scheming vampire that doesn't want those records getting out for reasons that have nothing to do with QAnon's dangerous bullshit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T18:32:44-07:00","id":1493035,"title":"","content":"Personally I think QAnon, or something similar to it, may work interestingly as a <i>medium</i> instead of an asset in itself.<br /> <br /> No supernatural created or control it, but in a world where the supernatural exists it certainly interacts with QAnon in some capacity. Some may try to use the boards and social networks to manipulate the tide of conspiracy, some may even try to pass off as Q, with varying degrees of success. Some profit from their limited relationship, some slip and end up in a mess of their own creation. Some are victims. And some are believers themselves.<br /> <br /> What potentially makes QAnon resistant to excessive supernatural interference is its decentralized nature. While stoking it is easy, controlling it to any direction but its natural nonsense is almost impossible, with new bullshit and crazy initiatives surfacing all the time.<br /> <br /> But I don't think Westboro should be ignored as also a relevant evil. It has caused an astounding amount of damage despite its size because of how the Phelps family learned to game the legal system in its favor. They basically live off (and well) from suing Topeka County all the frigging time, all the while constantly dancing atop the line between legal and illegal without ever crossing it, yet getting away with stuff you could swear to be illegal.<br /> <br /> Irl they're even in a sense helping, because many states developed better laws literally just to deal with Westboro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T19:41:49-07:00","id":1495400,"title":"","content":"This is the first time I've seen QAnon and Westboro mentioned on the internet without the flinging of poo.<br /> <br /> I try to stay away from modern politics in my games; though, most of the time it's not a problem. I do proxies of events, people and organization. XAnon anyone? <br /> <br /> I've gotten yelled at for even suggesting conspiracy theories; once, on RTalsorian's forums, I suggested an Cyberpunk game in which aliens are installing cybernetics on people captured on a military base, in the 1990s. They did not like that.<br /> <br /> One thing to consider is that people that are in those organizations are mentally-ill, and probably have done more meth than everyone on this board so they have a not-so-healthy paranoia. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T09:07:42-07:00","id":1495434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1495400#post1495400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first time I've seen QAnon and Westboro mentioned on the internet without the flinging of poo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there was a question with a relatively simple answer. Also, I don't think there are many people trying to support said orgs on the board.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I try to stay away from modern politics in my games; though, most of the time it's not a problem. I do proxies of events, people and organization. XAnon anyone? </div> </div> </div>Changing one letter is... not really a particularly clever dodge, honestly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've gotten yelled at for even suggesting conspiracy theories; once, on RTalsorian's forums, I suggested an Cyberpunk game in which aliens are installing cybernetics on people captured on a military base, in the 1990s. They did not like that. </div> </div> </div>Probably because pretty much every conspiracy theory tends to circle back to anti-semitism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing to consider is that people that are in those organizations are mentally-ill, and probably have done more meth than everyone on this board so they have a not-so-healthy paranoia. </div> </div> </div>Maybe the latter, definitely not the former. It's entirely possible to be high on religious fanaticism, so meth is not particularly necessary. And it remains to be seen if QAnon is anything but a grifter stringing along conservatives for the evulz; that's not being mentally ill, though, that's just being a spoiled brat who does things because no one ever told them &quot;no&quot;. Much like 45, incidentally.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T13:34:17-07:00","id":1495490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1492849-ideas-how-qanon-or-westboro-translate-to-world-of-darkness?p=1495434#post1495434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Changing one letter is... not really a particularly clever dodge, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's was never clever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Probably because pretty much every conspiracy theory tends to circle back to anti-semitism. </div> </div> </div>Not in R.Tal's case; I think they were tired of dealing with Moon-conspirators. Maybe in Right-wing Western ideology.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-25T02:38:00-07:00","id":1495556,"title":"","content":"I remember a few years ago I read an article on a fan site (ex noctis?) which suggested that extremist groups are far more common in wod and the jaded nature of the setting means people are less likely to react or just outright snap if they do. With that in mind the baptist Church's are a dime a dozen and are either ignored or possibly to be targeted for retaliatory violence when they touch someone's nerve, step on another hate cults toes or are considered for 'acquisition' by one of the darker powers....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-25-2022, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-25T12:06:15-07:00","id":1495590,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how well supported that really is. While there can be debate over how prevalent extremist thoughts are on both extremes of any given political spectrum, the prevalence of organized radicalized extremists tends to be asymmetrical. Hatred also tends to be a strong unifying force for people, so seemingly incomprehensible alliances form between groups much more easily if they hate the same thing, than if they love the same thing.<br /> <br /> There just isn't the real world evidence to back up the idea that increased organized extremist groups in the WoD would have some sort of self-correcting aspect to it. While the rise of extremist groups will have some push back from their opposition that will include a level of fight fire with fire thinking, history shows a strong trend towards escalation (not steady, there will be peaks and valleys along the way) until there's a major inflection point. Adding supernatural influence is only going to exacerbate the matter. If the supernatural entities in question want to stop these groups, they need to focus on the root causes of why they form over directly dealing with individual groups; history shows that taking out one organization just means it will be replaced. If the supernaturals in question want to use these groups for their own causes, they need to keep these groups like they are, but that also comes with a history of backfiring on anyone that thinks that's a sustainable proposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}